-- title:
--   Newvector exponent at p bounded by vₚ(N)
-- statement:
--   Let $\varphi$ be a complex-valued function on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$ (the group [`AutomorphicForm.AdelicGL2`](def/AutomorphicForm_AdelicLsXi.html#L12) of the ring of integers of $\mathbb{Q}$), assume $\varphi \neq 0$, and let $N$ be a nonzero natural number. The level hypothesis `hlev` asks right invariance of $\varphi$ under the finite part only: for every $g$ in the subgroup [`NumberField.AdelicLevel.finiteLevelOne`](def/NumberField_AdelicLevel.html#L418) of $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the finite adeles attached to the ideal [`AdelicDock.ratLevel N`](def/AdelicDock_LocalEmbedding.html#L303) $= (N)$ — that is, $g$ and $g^{-1}$ both have matrices satisfying `IsLevelOneMatrix`, the level-zero congruence conditions together with the lower-right entry lying in $1 +$ the ideal ball of $(N)$ — and every $x$, one has $\varphi(x \cdot \iota(g)) = \varphi(x)$, where $\iota =$ [`AdelicDock.finEmbed`](def/AdelicDock_LocalEmbedding.html#L145) is the embedding of finite adelic matrices into adelic matrices with identity component at the infinite places. Let $p$ be a prime. The conclusion is that there is a natural number $c \le$ the exponent of $p$ in the factorisation of $N$ such that [`LocalNewvector.HasNewvectorConductor p (LocalNewvector.AdelicSpan φ) c`](def/LocalNewvector_ConductorDatum.html#L88) holds: in the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A})$-translates of the carrier class of $\varphi$, equipped with its $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_p)$-action, the subspace of vectors fixed by `padicK1 p c` is nonzero while, for every $m < c$, the subspace fixed by `padicK1 p m` is zero.
--
--   This is the local-newvector (conductor) bound at a prime $p$ for the local representation generated by an adelic function of finite-part level $N$: the $K_1$-conductor exponent exists and does not exceed $v_p(N)$; equality is not asserted, and indeed fails for non-minimal $N$. It is used to equip the adelic span of a newform, and of the weight-one lift of a dihedral form, with conductor data at each prime.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_LocalNewvector_AdelicSpan_exists_hasNewvectorConductor_le_factorization.lean

import Definitions.Def_LocalNewvector_AdelicSpanCarrier

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem LocalNewvector.AdelicSpan.exists_hasNewvectorConductor_le_factorization
    (φ : AutomorphicForm.AdelicGL2 (NumberField.RingOfIntegers ℚ) ℚ → ℂ) (hφ : φ ≠ 0) {N : ℕ} (hN : N ≠ 0)
    (hlev : ∀ g ∈ NumberField.AdelicLevel.finiteLevelOne (NumberField.RingOfIntegers ℚ) ℚ (AdelicDock.ratLevel N),
      ∀ x, φ (x * AdelicDock.finEmbed (NumberField.RingOfIntegers ℚ) ℚ g) = φ x)
    (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] :
    ∃ c : ℕ, c ≤ N.factorization p ∧
      LocalNewvector.HasNewvectorConductor p (LocalNewvector.AdelicSpan φ) c := by sorry
